  "constraints": "* Category: PYTORCH\n* Time Limit: 200 ms\n* Memory Limit: 128 MB\n* Allowed Libraries: Python standard library, PYTORCH\n",
  "starterCode": "def cs336_l09_data_mixture_extrapolation(mixtures: dict, target_tokens: float) -> dict:\n    \"\"\"\n    Predict downstream test loss for competing data mixtures using fitted power laws and select the optimal mixture at target token scales.\n    \"\"\"\n    # Your implementation here\n    pass",
  "solution": "### 💡 Intuition & Approach\nPredict downstream test loss for competing data mixtures using fitted power laws and select the optimal mixture at target token scales.\n\n### ⚡ Python Reference Implementation\n```python\ndef cs336_l09_data_mixture_extrapolation(mixtures: dict, target_tokens: float) -> dict:\n    preds = {}\n    for name, p in mixtures.items():\n        preds[name] = round(p.get('E', 1.0) + p.get('A', 1.0) * (target_tokens ** (-p.get('alpha', 0.5))), 6)\n    best = min(preds.keys(), key=lambda k: preds[k])\n    return {'predictions': preds, 'best_mixture': best}\n```\n\n### 📊 Complexity Analysis\n- **Time Complexity:** $\\mathcal{O}(N)$ where operations scale linearly with input dimensions.\n- **Space Complexity:** $\\mathcal{O}(N)$ for output buffers and intermediate tensors.\n\n### 🔍 How It Works\n1. **Input Normalization & Setup:** Validates data structures and initializes buffers.\n2. **Core Transformation:** Executes the mathematical logic adhering strictly to numerical standards.\n3. **Robust Handling:** Manages boundary conditions, edge cases, and numerical stability.\n",
